WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.929
One question I get a lot is, "How do you
bridge the gap between two completely

00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:06.660
different WHYs inside an organization?"
It's a good question it's especially

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.909
when you feel like you're working at
cross-purposes.

00:00:08.909 --> 00:00:09.990
Now if it's done properly,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.767
the WHY should be nested within something higher.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:15.600
So for example, the United States has a WHY.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.600
It's based on the Declaration of Independence, 
all men are created equal, right.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.460
Now within the United States, 
we have nested WHYs.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.200
Each state has a WHY,
each city has its own WHY.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.289
In other words, Los Angeles has a very different WHY from New York.

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:32.040
Some people belong in New York,
some people belong in Los Angeles.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.400
They are not the same.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.800
But they're both distinctly American, 
they belong in America.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.050
Los Angeles wouldn't make sense
in France, it just wouldn't make sense.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.120
So it's gonna be the same inside 
an organization.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.050
Operations may seem to have

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.200
a completely different WHY than marketing, 
for example.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.460
Just like Los Angeles or New York.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.640
You either belong here or you
belong there.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.400
But they should both feel like they fit in the
overarching WHY.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.900
And that's actually how you 
find common ground.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.820
So when you feel like you're working at
cross-purposes,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.320
the opportunity is to actually take it
up a level. In other words, you say,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.729
hey, remember the WHY of this organization,
remember why this organization exists,

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:09.210
and we're both serving to advance that cause.
So that means we're working together,

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.300
we are cooperative.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.750
So whenever you find that you're at each other

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.439
because you have different WHYs or 
you feel like they're competing,

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:19.153
try and re-articulate that competition 
as to cooperative.

00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:20.369
We're cooperating together,

00:01:20.369 --> 00:01:24.000
serving different ways, 
in order to advance the greater good.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.543
And that's how you find cooperation

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:28.800
with seeming competitive WHYs 
inside the same organization.

